{"_id":"697d3e3f19b7a824528a457b","nodeId":"p0JHL8iAcV5tRLX9DPhx6","roadmapSlug":"ruby-on-rails","createdAt":"2026-01-30T23:26:55.240Z","description":"# Nested Forms\n\nNested forms allow you to manage associated models directly within a parent form. This means you can create, update, and delete records of related models on the same page as the parent model, providing a more streamlined user experience. For example, you might create a new blog post and its associated comments all at once.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Building Complex Forms","url":"https://guides.rubyonrails.org/form_helpers.html#building-complex-forms","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a18b"},{"type":"article","title":"Rails ΓÇö Nested Forms and Nested Resources","url":"https://david-rafe.medium.com/rails-nested-forms-and-nested-resources-cb9f21bb1a1a","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a18c"},{"type":"article","title":"Nested Forms in Rails - FastRuby.io","url":"https://www.fastruby.io/blog/learning/rails/nested-forms.html","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a18d"},{"type":"article","title":"Dynamic Nested Forms with Rails and Stimulus","url":"https://jonathanyeong.com/writing/rails-stimulus-dynamic-nested-form/","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a18e"},{"type":"video","title":"Rails - Nested Forms in Rails | [Tutorial]","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=niLRlaL-ss0","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a18f"},{"type":"video","title":"Stimulus Nested Forms | Ruby on Rails 7 Tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7JNRZLTRDCc","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a190"}],"updatedAt":"2026-01-30T23:26:55.240Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby-on-rails/content/p0JHL8iAcV5tRLX9DPhx6.md"}